  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ee48f05d3bb249aa987f5fdc1afbeee2",
      "statement": "OutboxPoller is the outbound-only bridge to a GMweb-API server: the phone dials out over HTTPS to a fixed URL — no tunnel, inbound port, or static IP — and the server hands over one queued send per request, delivered through the local EveSmsQueue, with the outcome acked so the server's ledger updates.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/GatewayPreferences.kt#L246-L249",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c24c958452b2f048bf8b01792e1995729c16d7d85d22e4cc1bbaa5489320886:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L21-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:188be4e7a63193c9f75cbe71650e9c6e601acce9a308ed1beade611a16fc061c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_81606e5963cd44549538fd58d6c36916",
      "statement": "The pull transport is a long-poll GET {gmwebUrl}/gateway/pull?waitMs=25000 (server holds ~25s when the queue is empty) returning {\"task\":null} or {\"task\":{requestId,to,text,priority}}; results are acked with POST {gmwebUrl}/gateway/ack, and every request carries the phone's gateway API key as X-API-Key, matching the GMweb server's GMWEB_ANDROID_DEVICE_KEY.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L156-L172",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e798249d73e7bc98acd98b8a08406f66ba6c4928319897e82c249f5eb6c3ca8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L190-L224",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4cb1d61aa1810aaf5c28ca0787e263578d624c61b43cdf7cc4ac82b6e3ab1c9a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L29-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f12a43ff8f71bc248fae58c4a5bea8e5796087dab70c62372b19fe8089cd337:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/release-v2.1.1.md#L12-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:daa5cc627f1bc8d42f56f67c827b1466e8c7cb18674dac15fe6622d32143ae05:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d784da76262a414088a2dd9ff60533d3",
      "statement": "A polled task is delivered through the same EveSmsQueue used by the LAN /send endpoint — enqueued with a null idempotency key (the server already de-duplicates), unknown priority defaulting to announcement — then drained until the record reaches a terminal status within a 120s deadline via drainUntilTerminal, which drives drainOne and polls status.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/eve/EveSmsQueue.kt#L233-L261",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d054cc853ebf7ad8ec7b8f54b93d822e9abcbf4b2de0c0adceb21d791ab143b8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L143-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b71e046cb0880fc18dd9f0c4d56d617c0d7f0df378e6cae2517f6a75afcbffcb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L174-L188",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2cfc6477c1b8dd12dd8fa2a7dc6caf69a13f9e1cfef8674ee01cfcd2d8d23acf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c425c76d3f0d4b0fbeed046263c14ac5",
      "statement": "The ack reports ok=true on success or ok=false with reason device_send_failed on delivery failure/timeout, and a lost ack is deliberately not re-sent locally — the GMweb server times the task out and owns the retry, so the phone must never re-send.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L151-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38dd02e83ee5ecb031395a40451caf24a4af257a4e568cf470b9f67e07a1ed9b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L190-L208",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4eb2b9fbfe7f34ebc64fd6cbe57969cd609fbf6a04333557aba901bab23d9943:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e19a930585ad4e25a418fcfde5b3a8be",
      "statement": "Because the queue's sender lambda is { to, text -> smsSender.sendForResult(to, text) != null } (installed by GatewayServer.start), a modem/SIM rejection returns a real false, the record becomes FAILED, and the ack reports device_send_failed — the same radio-level honesty the LAN path provides.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/GatewayServer.kt#L111-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:903e9380f41737a89de62d8d3b0eedf0ced4c34f7413eebdb39ff14aab339e92:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/sms/SmsSender.kt#L119-L134",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f06f63350bba7f8bcbde21788ab54712d0dafc41456d9b794999dd904a32799:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2ce47ae383c9470aa682e8224f5d098e",
      "statement": "The bridge is active whenever GatewayPreferences.gmwebUrl is non-blank; the setter requires an https:// prefix (rejecting plaintext) and treats an empty value as 'bridge disabled', while the LAN and cloud features keep working regardless.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/ConnectionSupervisor.kt#L255-L258",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af280319cdf4e82028bab1751e4df50a1893177261f88532bc1583be074e1055:"
        },
