    {
      "id": "claim_130881d8b2b14cd1b094f0455da7082f",
      "statement": "Each poll loop iteration gates on GatewayAccessPolicy.canTransmit(hasGatewayConsent, isEnabled) (versioned consent AND runtime enabled) and breaks to IDLE if either is false, so a revoked-consent or supervisor-stopped gateway stops polling even if the service process still lives.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/GatewayAccessPolicy.kt#L3-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f67674d766a6e07f50363e9e321df1cacef5acb6e511bade22ef79993c38e2c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L93-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d53b6247a7a6ca56f73f8bd92a207133af278332e965ef89ef6bbd7afa01f17c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2f764d9c30045d8b2692d93d804d92c",
      "statement": "Before each cycle the poller requires a validated network route (NetworkMonitor.isOnline); while offline it suspends on onlineFlow().first{online} so it makes zero HTTP requests against a dead radio, waking the instant the network returns (event-driven via a NetworkCallback flow, not a poll timer).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/NetworkMonitor.kt#L42-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6813134af8f00da253308f3f77663c57c51a9a0b100877e0f9a7615a183443c:"
        },
        {
